1
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:06,601
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:06,946 --> 00:00:09,706
I am going to get so drunk tonight.

3
00:00:09,706 --> 00:00:11,656
Like, way more than usual.

4
00:00:11,656 --> 00:00:12,650
[helicopter whirring, missiles whistling]
YEAH!

5
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:14,341
[helicopter whirring, missiles whistling]
IT'S THE SURFACE!

6
00:00:14,341 --> 00:00:15,605
[explosion, machine gun fire]
PARTY! P--

7
00:00:15,605 --> 00:00:18,469
[machine gun fire]
Dammit! It's the Fun Police!

8
00:00:18,469 --> 00:00:21,535
I'M ON YOUR SIDE, YOU FUCKING IDIOTS!

9
00:00:21,535 --> 00:00:25,701
HOW MANY OF YOU DO I HAVE TO
KILL BEFORE YOU UNDERSTAND THAT?!

10
00:00:26,869 --> 00:00:28,776
GODDAMN, YOU'RE STUPID!

11
00:00:28,776 --> 00:00:32,290
YOU'RE LIKE A BUNCH OF LEMMINGS
WITH MACHINE GUNS!

12
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:34,249
[explosions]
DO I LOOK LIKE AN ALIEN?!

13
00:00:34,249 --> 00:00:35,465
AM I GREEN?!

14
00:00:35,465 --> 00:00:37,852
DO I HAVE TENTACLES COMING OUT OF ME?!

15
00:00:37,852 --> 00:00:38,847
GIVE ME THIS!

16
00:00:38,847 --> 00:00:39,759
AND THIS!

17
00:00:39,759 --> 00:00:41,258
Wait, is that a chopper?

18
00:00:41,258 --> 00:00:42,709
HEY, HEY, HEY!

19
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:44,202
HHHHEEEELLLLP!

20
00:00:44,202 --> 00:00:45,573
HELP ME!

21
00:00:45,573 --> 00:00:47,100
[explosions]
WHAT THE FUCK?!

22
00:00:48,038 --> 00:00:49,783
[explosions]
WHY ARE WE BOMBING?!

23
00:00:49,783 --> 00:00:51,743
THERE'S NOBODY HERE!

24
00:00:51,743 --> 00:00:54,707
WHY ARE THE SOLDIERS
BOMBING EACH OTHER?!

25
00:00:54,707 --> 00:00:56,295
IS THIS REAL?!

26
00:00:56,295 --> 00:00:58,555
I JUST WANT TO GO HOME!

27
00:00:58,555 --> 00:01:01,200
EVERYONE IS CRAZY EXCEPT ME!

28
00:01:01,878 --> 00:01:02,767
[machine gun fire]
AGH!

29
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:04,618
I DON'T UNDERSTAND!

30
00:01:04,618 --> 00:01:07,113
WHY IS EVERYONE TRYING TO KILL ME?!

31
00:01:07,113 --> 00:01:08,494
I'M AWESOME!

32
00:01:08,494 --> 00:01:10,437
ARE YOU ALL JEALOUS?!

33
00:01:10,437 --> 00:01:12,925
SHOOTING AT PEOPLE ISN'T VERY NICE!

34
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:14,822
GIVE PEACE A CHANCE!

35
00:01:14,822 --> 00:01:16,667
OR AT LEAST, STAND STILL!

36
00:01:16,667 --> 00:01:17,594
[missiles whistling, explosions]

37
00:01:17,594 --> 00:01:20,773
[missiles whistling]
Oh God, more bombs, more bombs, more bombs...

38
00:01:20,773 --> 00:01:23,380
[explosions]
QUIT RAINING ON MY PARADE!

39
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:24,449
[explosions]
THIS IS BULLSHIT!

40
00:01:24,449 --> 00:01:27,593
THIS IS WHY WE HAVE A SECURITY DEPARTMENT!

41
00:01:27,593 --> 00:01:28,947
[machine gun fire]
AGH!

42
00:01:28,947 --> 00:01:31,473
TO PREVENT THINGS LIKE THIS FROM HAPPENING!

43
00:01:31,473 --> 00:01:33,661
[missiles whistling]
SOMEBODY'S NOT DOING THEIR JOB!

44
00:01:33,661 --> 00:01:35,113
[explosions]
Ehhh...

45
00:01:35,113 --> 00:01:39,205
[explosions]
THIS IS THE WORST RESCUE OPERATION IN HISTORY!

46
00:01:39,205 --> 00:01:41,207
I'M REPORTING ALL OF YOU!

47
00:01:41,207 --> 00:01:44,367
I'LL COME BACK AND GET YOUR
NAMES ONCE THE BOMBING'S OVER!

48
00:01:44,367 --> 00:01:46,434
[missiles whistling, explosions]
Climbfastclimbfastclimbfastclimbfast...

49
00:01:46,434 --> 00:01:47,851
[missiles whistling, explosions]

50
00:01:47,851 --> 00:01:49,819
Okay, anyone following me this time?

51
00:01:49,819 --> 00:01:50,667
I'm ready.

52
00:01:51,029 --> 00:01:52,000
I'm ready.

53
00:01:52,374 --> 00:01:53,000
No...

54
00:01:53,418 --> 00:01:54,067
All right.

55
00:01:55,409 --> 00:01:57,831
God, I'm back underground again!

56
00:01:57,831 --> 00:01:59,736
I COULD'VE BEEN OUT OF HERE!

57
00:01:59,736 --> 00:02:00,500
BUT, NO!

58
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,521
The fucking Army or
whatever is trying to kill me,

59
00:02:03,521 --> 00:02:06,212
and they're bombing the surface
for no God damned reason!

60
00:02:06,212 --> 00:02:08,661
They don't even care if they hit
their own troops!

61
00:02:08,661 --> 00:02:11,477
I-I just don't understand
anything anymore.

62
00:02:11,477 --> 00:02:12,856
[missiles whistling, explosions]
I just want to get out of here

63
00:02:12,856 --> 00:02:16,239
and let everybody else go crazy
with each other on their own time.

64
00:02:16,239 --> 00:02:17,576
Not mine!

65
00:02:17,576 --> 00:02:19,616
What's this? "Vent Access"?

66
00:02:19,616 --> 00:02:20,645
Yeah, I don't know if I wanna--

67
00:02:20,645 --> 00:02:21,526
[explosion]

68
00:02:21,526 --> 00:02:23,396
Well, that's nice. Now I have options.

69
00:02:23,396 --> 00:02:27,340
I can have death-from-above this way
or death-from-above the other way.

70
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:29,067
And there's another bug...

71
00:02:30,597 --> 00:02:32,067
Let's see... there he is!

72
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:35,000
That's right, run!  RUN!

73
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:37,878
Dammit, this isn't working.

74
00:02:37,878 --> 00:02:40,018
See, this is why I needed that shotgun.

75
00:02:40,018 --> 00:02:42,438
It has good spread and stopping power.

76
00:02:42,438 --> 00:02:44,970
It's practically designed
to kill roaches.

77
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:47,550
Wow, what's the point of having
an underground bunker

78
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:49,300
if we can just blow a hole in the top?

79
00:02:51,757 --> 00:02:54,530
Oh, they're using steel grates here.

80
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:58,851
Not those cheap-ass...
aluminum ones I've been running into.

81
00:02:58,851 --> 00:03:02,296
Dammit, I don't even want to
think about the irony of this.

82
00:03:02,296 --> 00:03:04,474
And how I'm trying to go back--

83
00:03:04,474 --> 00:03:09,460
How I'm trying to go back underground even
though all I want is to get out of here.

84
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:13,854
Well, actually, I want a lot of
things, but number one on the list

85
00:03:13,854 --> 00:03:15,228
was getting out of here.

86
00:03:15,228 --> 00:03:19,562
But, now that we're blowing up the surface
of the Earth, that changes my priorities.

87
00:03:19,562 --> 00:03:22,607
This must've been what
H.G. Wells was talking about.

88
00:03:22,607 --> 00:03:26,384
Maybe half of humanity will go
underground and start a new society--

89
00:03:26,384 --> 00:03:27,358
...careful....

90
00:03:27,358 --> 00:03:29,768
--and enslave the surface-dwellers.

91
00:03:29,768 --> 00:03:31,405
That's my destiny.

92
00:03:31,405 --> 00:03:34,740
Yeah. I'm a first-generation Morlock.

93
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:38,007
I don't think I'll start cannibalizing
people right away, though.

94
00:03:38,007 --> 00:03:40,728
I'll at least wait until the
vending machines run out.

95
00:03:40,728 --> 00:03:42,588
Man, somebody's laughing at me.

96
00:03:42,588 --> 00:03:45,725
Perfectly good shotgun ammo
and I can't use it.

97
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:50,334
I guess I can't complain. I have other
guns, but can you really have too many?

98
00:03:51,149 --> 00:03:52,334
Wait a minute...

99
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:55,940
That's that cargo hook I've swung on.

100
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:58,878
I've been here before!

101
00:03:58,878 --> 00:04:01,085
[groans]

102
00:04:01,085 --> 00:04:02,718
All right, all right.

103
00:04:02,718 --> 00:04:04,753
Well, I'm just going to keep
moving forward.

104
00:04:04,753 --> 00:04:10,298
I'm not ready to believe this entire
facility is a giant fucking Möbius strip.

105
00:04:10,298 --> 00:04:12,840
Maybe I should become a
tour guide after this.

106
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:15,250
I'm good at acting like I know
where the hell I'm going.

107
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:16,627
"Follow me."

108
00:04:16,627 --> 00:04:18,734
[headcrab squeals, bites]
RAGH! STOP THAT!

109
00:04:19,388 --> 00:04:20,936
YOU CAN'T FOLLOW ME!

110
00:04:20,936 --> 00:04:22,194
YOU DON'T HAVE ANY MONEY!

111
00:04:22,194 --> 00:04:24,010
THAT'S THE WHOLE POINT!

112
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:26,507
Where the hell did you
come from, anyway?

113
00:04:26,507 --> 00:04:28,378
Oh...

114
00:04:28,378 --> 00:04:32,437
This must be the right way as
opposed to my way.

115
00:04:32,437 --> 00:04:34,487
Y'know, the thing that
bugs me about today

116
00:04:34,487 --> 00:04:37,185
is that I seem to be making all
the right decisions

117
00:04:37,185 --> 00:04:40,906
but my situation has been
getting really dangerous.

118
00:04:40,906 --> 00:04:41,469
I don't--

119
00:04:41,469 --> 00:04:47,569
HECU: I killed twelve dumbass scientists
and not one of them fought back. This sucks.

120
00:04:47,569 --> 00:04:51,571
Yeah, I guess that's what happens when
you shoot everyone on a rescue operation.

121
00:04:51,571 --> 00:04:55,659
But, not to worry, I'm a scientist
and I'm armed like a secessionist.

122
00:04:55,659 --> 00:04:56,649
Hey, that rhymes.

123
00:04:56,649 --> 00:04:58,490
[machine gun fire]
AGH! OKAY, FINE!

124
00:04:58,490 --> 00:04:59,196
[machine gun fire]
I SHOULD'VE KNOWN

125
00:04:59,196 --> 00:05:01,033
[machine gun fire]
YOU GUYS AREN'T INTO POETRY!

126
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,406
I guess I can't completely blame you.

127
00:05:03,406 --> 00:05:05,934
That wasn't a perfect rhyme;
the syllable count was off.

128
00:05:06,413 --> 00:05:07,224
So, what's that make?

129
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:10,913
Twelve... fifteen counts of self-defense
with an automatic weapon?

130
00:05:10,913 --> 00:05:14,358
I'm losing count and I don't think the
cops are going to buy that anymore.

131
00:05:14,358 --> 00:05:17,207
I'd better just keep quiet
about this when I get out.

132
00:05:17,207 --> 00:05:20,534
I'll have to fight my urges to
brag about it when I get a new job.

133
00:05:21,277 --> 00:05:22,767
Have I been here, too?

134
00:05:24,097 --> 00:05:27,407
I don't know. This place starts
looking the same after a while.

135
00:05:27,407 --> 00:05:30,601
It's just some never-ending
fantasy warehouse.

136
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:32,133
No...

137
00:05:34,024 --> 00:05:36,033
I want some Cheetos.

138
00:05:36,033 --> 00:05:38,333
All right, back in this snake hole.

139
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:42,638
This must've been what it was like
for the Viet Cong, underground all the time,

140
00:05:42,638 --> 00:05:44,530
crawling around in cramped tunnels,

141
00:05:44,530 --> 00:05:46,747
American soldiers shooting at you,

142
00:05:46,747 --> 00:05:47,334
bugs...

143
00:05:47,924 --> 00:05:50,030
I can't believe it's evening already.

144
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:52,014
Is it Daylight Savings Time?

145
00:05:52,014 --> 00:05:54,177
No, wait, that wouldn't affect the sky.

146
00:05:54,177 --> 00:05:56,317
I hate Daylight Savings Time.

147
00:05:56,317 --> 00:05:58,016
Uh, this way.

148
00:05:58,016 --> 00:06:01,674
Daylight Savings Time is just another
sanction employed by The Man

149
00:06:01,674 --> 00:06:03,025
to keep us down.

150
00:06:03,025 --> 00:06:05,639
The Founding Fathers didn't have
Daylight Savings Time

151
00:06:05,639 --> 00:06:07,000
and there's a reason for that.

152
00:06:08,624 --> 00:06:10,801
All right, this looks like a cafeteria,

153
00:06:11,266 --> 00:06:13,747
except we're serving up
batteries and ammo.

154
00:06:13,747 --> 00:06:14,701
That's weird.

155
00:06:16,307 --> 00:06:18,688
I still don't know where I am.

156
00:06:18,688 --> 00:06:21,744
Never thought I'd say this but I
think I have enough bullets for now.

157
00:06:21,744 --> 00:06:25,763
And it seems we have an airtight freezer
with no way to open it from the other side.

158
00:06:25,763 --> 00:06:27,346
Kind of a bad omen.

159
00:06:27,346 --> 00:06:30,801
Not to say that anything has
been encouraging about this day.

160
00:06:31,591 --> 00:06:32,143
[lock buzzes]

161
00:06:32,143 --> 00:06:33,614
And this door's locked.

162
00:06:33,614 --> 00:06:35,631
Okay, fuck you too, room.

163
00:06:35,631 --> 00:06:37,100
Back to my life as a mole.

164
00:06:37,589 --> 00:06:39,290
You know, this might suck.

165
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:43,315
If they ever polygraphed me at another
job and ask if I'm a mole at the company,

166
00:06:43,315 --> 00:06:45,782
I'll know what they mean,
but at the same time,

167
00:06:45,782 --> 00:06:48,575
I know I'm going to hesitate or
panic or something

168
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:52,052
because I'll be thinking back to right
now where I'm spending my whole day

169
00:06:52,052 --> 00:06:53,756
crawling underground in the dark

170
00:06:53,756 --> 00:06:55,328
and it'll trip up the polygraph.

171
00:06:55,328 --> 00:06:56,200
I know it.

172
00:06:58,549 --> 00:07:00,834
See, there's another vent.
This isn't going to end.

173
00:07:02,164 --> 00:07:03,434
Ah, there we go.

174
00:07:03,849 --> 00:07:06,785
Y'know, that's not to say that I
wouldn't be the other kind of mole, too,

175
00:07:06,785 --> 00:07:08,676
but nobody's made me any offers.

176
00:07:08,676 --> 00:07:12,958
I would've sold out Black Mesa a long
time ago if it meant I could retire early.

177
00:07:12,958 --> 00:07:15,317
We have BIG trade secrets.

178
00:07:15,317 --> 00:07:15,850
Oh, what the--

179
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:16,634
SCIENTIST: Fascinating.

180
00:07:17,277 --> 00:07:20,011
SCIENTIST: I never suspected such things could be.
Oh...

181
00:07:20,011 --> 00:07:22,528
It's those two zombies again!

182
00:07:22,528 --> 00:07:25,069
I'm going around in circles!

183
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:26,568
Big circles!

184
00:07:26,568 --> 00:07:27,848
This is pathetic.

185
00:07:27,848 --> 00:07:30,270
Those two have gotten more
done just standing there

186
00:07:30,270 --> 00:07:33,980
than I have running all over this
facility leaving a trail of bodies.

187
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:36,372
SCIENTIST: I predicted all of
this, you know.  All of it.

188
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:37,574
This is horrible.

189
00:07:37,574 --> 00:07:39,400
I'm just... gonna get out of here.

190
00:07:41,522 --> 00:07:43,443
I wonder what Freud
would've said about me

191
00:07:43,443 --> 00:07:45,991
about crawling in and out of all
these ventilation shafts.

192
00:07:45,991 --> 00:07:47,608
Nothing good, I bet.

193
00:07:47,608 --> 00:07:50,742
Freud was kind of a nutbar, but
you have to give him some props.

194
00:07:50,742 --> 00:07:52,382
He had the perfect angle.

195
00:07:52,382 --> 00:07:54,734
He made all these theories you
couldn't disprove.

196
00:07:55,859 --> 00:07:56,267
C'mon!

197
00:07:58,810 --> 00:08:00,569
But, yeah, he could say
anything he wanted

198
00:08:00,569 --> 00:08:03,926
then claim you repressed the
memories of what he was talking about.

199
00:08:03,926 --> 00:08:05,534
It's an unbeatable strategy.

200
00:08:07,395 --> 00:08:08,367
C'mon, c'mon!

201
00:08:11,004 --> 00:08:11,534
Oh.

202
00:08:12,229 --> 00:08:14,938
Yeah, I wish I had a "theory" like that.

203
00:08:14,938 --> 00:08:17,576
You can't get away with that
kind of crap in physics.

204
00:08:17,576 --> 00:08:20,667
You have to have serious
math to back it up.

205
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,831
Well, except for the string
theory crowd.

206
00:08:22,831 --> 00:08:25,142
Those guys are a bunch of cultists.

207
00:08:25,142 --> 00:08:27,767
I think Steve and Richard
sacrificed goats.

208
00:08:27,767 --> 00:08:30,186
That's why they never let me
come to their cookouts.

209
00:08:30,186 --> 00:08:32,000
They've called the cops on me before.

210
00:08:32,599 --> 00:08:35,686
It's too bad I didn't know about
all these ventilation shafts earlier.

211
00:08:35,686 --> 00:08:37,107
I could've used them to
crawl around and

212
00:08:37,107 --> 00:08:39,635
scare the hell out of people in
their offices.

213
00:08:39,635 --> 00:08:42,267
Y'know, just whisper stuff
when it's dark and quiet.

214
00:08:42,635 --> 00:08:43,734
"I'm watching."

215
00:08:44,088 --> 00:08:47,703
Then I can spread some rumor about how
some guy got killed there and it's haunted

216
00:08:47,703 --> 00:08:49,570
and maybe take the office for myself.

217
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:50,701
It would've been sweet.

218
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:52,901
Oh no...

219
00:08:53,990 --> 00:08:55,133
I give up.

220
00:08:57,525 --> 00:08:59,400
Guess I'll just die here.

